{
  "title": "Luna Home Co. Service Menu, Pricing & Software Stack Development",
  "content": "This plan develops three deliverables for Luna Home Co. in parallel: (1) a detailed service menu with tiered pricing tailored to Austin's 78701/78704/78745 market and busy professionals/young families, (2) a pricing strategy designed to maximize recurring client conversion, and (3) a booking/invoicing software recommendation within the $75/mo budget. Each deliverable is researched and drafted independently, then synthesized into a final cohesive document.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Research Austin TX residential cleaning market rates in detail for zip codes 78701, 78704, 78745. Find competitor pricing for standard recurring cleans (weekly/biweekly/monthly), deep cleans, move-in/move-out cleans, and common add-ons. Focus on services targeting busy professionals and young families. Include at least 5 competitor examples with specific pricing.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research and compare booking/invoicing software options specifically suited for a 3-person residential cleaning team doing 25-35 cleanings/month, with a strict budget of under $75/month total. Evaluate: (1) Jobber, (2) Housecall Pro, (3) ZenMaid, (4) Launch27/BookingKoala, (5) Square Appointments + Wave/Invoice Ninja combo. For each, find current 2025/2026 pricing tiers, features relevant to cleaning services (online booking/quote forms, automated reminders, intake questions for sq ft/beds/baths/pets, calendar sync, payment processing, basic CRM/client notes), pros/cons, and any cleaning-industry-specific advantages. Recommend the top 2-3 options with reasoning.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Research best practices for residential cleaning service pricing strategy that maximizes recurring client conversion and reduces one-off jobs. Cover: (1) How to structure Good/Better/Best tiered service packages for cleaning, (2) Optimal discount structures for weekly vs biweekly vs monthly recurring plans, (3) How to price deep cleans and move-in/move-out to encourage conversion to recurring, (4) Add-on pricing psychology (bundled vs a-la-carte), (5) Strategies for same-day/priority surcharges, (6) Minimum visit charges and cancellation fee best practices, (7) How to handle square footage tiers (e.g., <1000 sqft, 1000-2000, 2000-3000, 3000+). Provide specific percentage ranges and real-world examples from successful cleaning businesses.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_sub_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Synthesize all research into a comprehensive, actionable deliverable for Luna Home Co. with three sections:\n\n**Section 1 - Service Menu**: Create a complete, formatted service menu with specific dollar amounts for each service tier (Standard Recurring in weekly/biweekly/monthly frequencies, Deep Clean/First-Time Reset, Move-In/Move-Out) broken down by home size (1-2 bed, 3 bed, 4+ bed or by square footage tiers). Include a full add-on menu with prices (inside fridge, inside oven, interior windows, laundry fold, dishes, baseboards, pet hair treatment, same-day/priority surcharge). Price competitively for central Austin targeting busy professionals/young families.\n\n**Section 2 - Pricing Strategy**: Document the pricing logic including recurring discount structure (e.g., 15% off weekly, 10% off biweekly vs one-time rate), first-clean incentive pricing, cancellation/late-cancel policy, minimum visit charge, referral discount program, and seasonal pricing adjustments. Include specific tactics to convert one-off deep cleans into recurring clients.\n\n**Section 3 - Software Stack Recommendation**: Recommend the best software stack within $75/mo budget with a primary recommendation and backup option. Include setup steps, estimated monthly cost breakdown, and which features map to Luna Home Co.'s specific needs (online quote form, automated reminders, intake questions, calendar sync, payment processing, CRM/notes).",
      "tool_name": "reasoning",
      "depends_on": [0, 1, 2]
    }
  ],
